<title>USA: Ecuador wins most oil contractors assent on prices.</title>
<headline>Ecuador wins most oil contractors assent on prices.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's state oil company Petroecuador has agreed price changes with most of its term contract customers, though its sole buyer in Asia has yet to agree and one of its U.S. contractors dropped out.</p>
<p>The new prices, which apply from May 1, effectively result in a 30/40 cents increase in the relative price for buyers bringing Ecuadoran Oriente to the U.S. East Coast, Gulf and to the Caribbean, traders said.</p>
</text>
